WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.920
Let's touch base with our color from the five
one seven area code before we run out of time.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:13.730
Who's calling today from five one seven five
one seven.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.970
Are we muted?

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.160
No, you're not.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.160
What's going on?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.160
Five one seven.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.160
[inaudible] are you there David?

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.210
Yes, I am.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.730
You there, David?

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.250
Yes, I am.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.269
Uh, hi.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:35.000
I was calling in today to ask you, what do
you think we can do to combat cognitive dissonance

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
within the liberal party, the liberal.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.350
And I find that whenever a lot of people like
that last call, or bringing facts to people,

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:50.400
if they talk red mining, if you want to bring
up Obama droning the hell out of the middle

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.720
East and starting new legal Wars, if you want
to bring up the poisoning of our water for

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.850
four decades, three decades, excuse me, three
decades by almost every single president with

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.640
open munitions burnings, people just closed
down.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.359
It's not just the right, like people want
to think the left is in a state right now.

00:01:09.359 --> 00:01:11.330
We're, we're closing down as well.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:15.200
We don't want to hear the facts if they don't
conform to our worlds.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.409
Do you want our bubbles?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:24.500
So what can we do on the left to try to bring
our own side back to, I might not like these

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.150
facts, but the facts.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.150
Yeah.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.310
Listen, I mean, I, we can only do this at
the individual level.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.970
Uh, I regularly make it a point on this program
to say I'm on the left.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.189
The program leans left.

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:39.389
I think that the left is right on way more
issues than the right.

00:01:39.389 --> 00:01:44.299
But there's issues where Republicans and Democrats
are both guilty of almost the same thing to

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:46.179
almost the exact same extent.

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:49.619
I mean, you can't do anything other than to
tell the truth.

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:53.340
And this is more of a, of a behavioral economics
issue.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.630
It's a psychology issue.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.570
It's more than partisan.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.600
But being aware of it is step one and step
two is pointing it out when we see it.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.759
And you know, I try to do that every day.

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:07.750
So do you think that there's much hope for
things getting better?

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.750
Yeah, I have hope.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.679
I mean that's one issue where I am optimistic.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:15.819
I think if we go back to teaching critical
thinking, uh, at an early age, if we teach

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:22.420
civics and philosophy starting in middle school,
I think that we will predispose people to

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.310
be less, um, uh, subject to the cognitive
dissonance you're talking about.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.569
That's my hope.

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:37.030
Where I would argue with you that you can
look in, people are willing to voice them.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.319
They're willing to put their wait, wait.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:42.390
They're willing to what?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.920
Okay.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.310
It looked like he said willing.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.060
Did he say willing to drink poison?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.450
I don't know.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:50.540
This is a problem.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.750
I'm trying to deal with it here and it requires
some bigger systemic solutions.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.750
That's all the time I have today.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.750
Sorry to everybody.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.920
I didn't get to quick rake much more right
after that.

